 "about_text": "Gagosian is a global gallery for modern and contemporary art founded by Larry Gagosian in Los Angeles in 1980. From that first space it has grown into a network of exhibition spaces across the United States, Europe, and Asia, designed by architects including Richard Meier, Jean Nouvel, and Selldorf Architects. The program pairs a roster of leading living artists working across painting, sculpture, photography, and design with museum-quality historical exhibitions of twentieth-century masters. The gallery also runs a publishing arm producing catalogues raisonnés, monographs, and the Gagosian Quarterly magazine, and has developed initiatives supporting artists' estates and legacy planning alongside talks, screenings, and studio-visit programming.",
